"""
A cookie recipe calls for the following ingredients:    
1.5 cups of sugar  1 cup of butter  2.75 cups of flour
The recipe produces 48 cookies with this amount of the ingredients. 
Write a program that asks the user how many cookies he or she wants to make, 
then displays the number of cups of each ingredient needed for the specified number of cookies.
"""
#Cookie recipe variables for a recipe of48 cookies 
cookie_batch = 48
sugar_cups = 1.5
butter_cups = 1
flour_cups = 2.75
#Gather input from user for amount of cookies to make 
input_cookies = int(input("How many cookies do you want to make? "))
#Divide the user input amount by the cookie batch and multiply for each ingredient
sugar_needed = float(input_cookies / cookie_batch) * sugar_cups
butter_needed = float(input_cookies / cookie_batch) * butter_cups
flour_needed = (input_cookies / cookie_batch) * flour_cups
#Output the amount of each ingredient needed to make the specified amount of cookies
print(f"To make {input_cookies} cookies, you will need: \n",
      f"{sugar_needed:.2f} cups of sugar, \n",
      f"{butter_needed:.2f} cups of butter, \n",
      f"and {flour_needed:.2f} cups of flour.")